.TH "ELEMENT.TOUCHMOVE_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.touchmove_event \- Element: touchmove event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]touchmove\f[R] event is fired when one or more touch points
are moved along the touch surface.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqtouchmove\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
ontouchmove = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]TouchEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Code samples for those events are available on the dedicated page: Touch
events.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Touch events
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]mousemove\f[R]
